    "full": "ˆXL on qubit 2 (Fig. 12d). We have now reached the terminal measurements at the end of the circuit. At this\n--- [Page 18] ---\n18\n〉\n〉\n(a)\n〉\n〉\n(b)\nIL\nIL\nXL\n〉\n〉\n(c) XL\nXL\n〉\n〉\n(d) ZL\nXL\n〉\n〉\n(e) -\nFIG. 12. (Color online) Example of how ˆZL and ˆXL operators\nare handled in the control software. Here we commute a ˆZL\nlogical operator (colored blue (light)) on one qubit with an\nidentity ˆIL (colored blue (light)) on a second qubit through a\nsequence of logical operations (colored black), here including\ntwo Hadamards and a CNOT, ending with a measurement\nof each qubit. (a) We start with ˆZL operating on qubit 1\nwith the ˆIL identity on qubit 2. (b) The two operations are\ncommuted one step to the right, with ˆZL transformed by the\nHadamard to an ˆXL. (c) The two operations are commuted\nthrough the CNOT, with ˆXL on qubit 1 remaining unchanged\nwhile ˆIL on the second qubit transforms to ˆXL."
