    "full": "logical CNOT, are all Cliﬀord gates except ˆTL\nand ˆT †\nL (see Ref. [47]). We discuss how to commute ˆXL and ˆZL\nthrough the ˆSL and ˆTL gates in Sect. XVI.\n--- [Page 19] ---\n19\n(a) (b)\nZL\nXL\nFIG. 13. (Color online) Easy initialization of an X-cut logical qubit. Using the logical qubit’s upper hole, the stable\nmeasure-X outcome just prior to creating the qubit hole by\nturning oﬀ the measure-X qubit is equal to the initial logical\neigenvalue of the qubit.\nthe strip will serve as one of the qubit holes. In addition,\nthe ˆZ stabilizers that border the strip are switched from\nmeasuring four adjacent data qubits to measuring just\nthree (by simply excluding one data qubit from the surface code CNOT cycle in Fig. 1). There are six ˆZ stabilizers that are switched from four- to three-terminal operation in Fig. 14b. 17 The three isolated data qubits (numbered 1, 2 and 3 in Fig. 14) are measured once along ˆZ to\nmaintain error correction, and then set to the ground |g⟩\nstate as in Fig. 14c. 18 Setting these three qubits to their\nground state ensures that the quiescent state |ψ⟩ will be\nin the logical ground state of the ˆZL = ˆZ1 ˆZ2 ˆZ3 operator. Finally the two ˆX stabilizers internal to the strip\nare turned back on, and the three-terminal ˆZ stabilizers\nswitched back to four-terminal measurements, completing the process."
