    "full": "ZL so that\nit encloses two stabilizer cells, its original cell plus the\none below it, by multiplying ˆZL by the four ˆZ operators,\nˆZ6 ˆZ7 ˆZ8 ˆZ9, that make up the ˆZ stabilizer below the qubit\nhole. We term the new extended operator ˆZ e\nL, which is\ngiven by\nˆZ e\nL = ( ˆZ3 ˆZ4 ˆZ5 ˆZ6) × ( ˆZ6 ˆZ7 ˆZ8 ˆZ9)\n= ˆZ3 ˆZ4 ˆZ5 ˆZ7 ˆZ8 ˆZ9,\n(17)\nas shown in Fig. 17a. We complete the ﬁrst surface code\ncycle of the move, turning oﬀ the lower ˆZ stabilizer and\nmeasuring data qubit 6. We redeﬁne the ˆXL operator by\nmultiplying it by ˆX6, giving\nˆX ′\nL = ˆX1 ˆX2 ˆX3 ˆX6; (18)\nZ4\nZ3\nZ6\nZ5\nX2\nX3\nX6\nZ7\nZ8\nZ97\n8\n9\nX1\nX2\nX3\nX1\nZ4\nZ3\nZ5\nX2\nX3\nX1\nX6\nZ7\nZ8\nZ9\nZ6\nZL\nXL\nZL\nXL’\n’\nZL\ne\n(a) (b) (c)\nFIG. 17. (Color online) Process for moving a Z-cut logical\nqubit hole vertically down by one cell in the 2D array. (a)\nLogical qubit with ˆXL = ˆX1 ˆX2 ˆX3 and ˆZL = ˆZ3 ˆZ4 ˆZ5 ˆZ6. (b)\nWe extend the ˆZL operator by multiplying it by the ˆZ stabilizer just below the lower qubit hole: ˆZ e\nL = ( ˆZ6 ˆZ7 ˆZ8 ˆZ9) ˆZL =\nˆZ3 ˆZ4 ˆZ5 ˆZ7 ˆZ8 ˆZ9. We next turn oﬀ this ˆZ stabilizer, and also\nturn the surrounding four-terminal ˆX stabilizers into threeterminal stabilizers, leaving data qubit 6 without any stabilizer measurements. We perform an ˆX measurement of\ndata qubit 6 (using either an idle measure-Z qubit, or directly measuring the data qubit, as shown). (c) We deﬁne the extended operator ˆX ′\nL by multiplying ˆXL by ˆX6:\nˆX ′\nL = ˆX6 ˆXL = ˆX1 ˆX2 ˆX3 ˆX6."
