    "snippet": "g in Eq. (20) is determined by whether\na sign change occurred in ˆXL during the move, with\npX = 0(1) if a sign change did not (did) occur; the power\npZ is determined similarly for sign changes in ˆZL. The\nbyproduct operator ˆZ ′\nL corrects the sign of the transformed ˆX ′\nL through their anti-commutation relation, and\nthe byproduct operator ˆX ′\nL similarly corrects ˆZ ′\nL.\nWe do not actually apply the byproduct operators as\nexplicit gates; instead, we simply track these additional\nˆXL and ˆZL o...",
    "full": "g in Eq. (20) is determined by whether\na sign change occurred in ˆXL during the move, with\npX = 0(1) if a sign change did not (did) occur; the power\npZ is determined similarly for sign changes in ˆZL. The\nbyproduct operator ˆZ ′\nL corrects the sign of the transformed ˆX ′\nL through their anti-commutation relation, and\nthe byproduct operator ˆX ′\nL similarly corrects ˆZ ′\nL.\nWe do not actually apply the byproduct operators as\nexplicit gates; instead, we simply track these additional\nˆXL and ˆZL operators in the control software, as discussed in Sect. IX. These corrective operators are thus\nonly applied when the logical qubit is measured, reversing the sign of a ˆZL measurement if that qubit has an\nˆXL byproduct operator, and reversing the sign of an ˆXL\nmeasurement if that qubit has a ˆZL byproduct operator. Two corrective ˆXLs or two corrective ˆZLs cancel, as\nˆX 2\nL = ˆZ 2\nL = ˆIL.\nWe can also look at what happens to our description of the 2D array wavefunction |ψ⟩ in terms of the\nstabilizer and logical qubit subspaces. Prior to the\nmove, we have |ψ⟩ = |Q⟩|qL⟩; after the move, we have\nˆX ′pZ\nL ˆZ ′pX\nL |ψ′⟩ = ˆX ′pZ\nL ˆZ ′pX\nL |Q′⟩|q′\nL⟩, where |Q′⟩|q′\nL⟩ is the\ndesired state. The byproduct operators only aﬀect the\nlogical state, so we can write the equivalent to Eq. (20)\nas\n|qL⟩ → ˆX ′pZ\nL ˆZ ′pX\nL |q′\nL⟩, (21)\nwhere |q′\nL⟩ is the desired logical state.\nC. Multi-cell logical qubit move\nWe can easily generalize the one-cell move to a multicell move."
