    "full": "ves special ancilla states. Implementing ˆSL relies on\nthe |YL⟩ ancilla state\n|YL⟩ = 1\n√\n2 (|gL⟩ +i|eL⟩), (45)\nwhile implementing ˆTL relies on the |AL⟩ ancilla state\n|AL⟩ = 1√\n2\n(\n|gL⟩ +eiπ/4|eL⟩\n)\n. (46)\nThe |YL⟩ and |AL⟩ ancilla states are created in a special “short qubit,” which can be put in an arbitrary but\nconcomitantly imperfect state, a process known as “state\ninjection.” Once the state has been injected, the “short\nqubit” is increased to the standard distance d to make\nit less error-prone, and the imperfect logical state of the\nstandard-distance qubit is then puriﬁed by a high-ﬁdelity\nprocess known as “distillation”; we discuss these steps\nbelow. The ˆSL and ˆTL gates are then implemented with\ncircuits using logical CNOTs and Hadamards involving\nthese ancilla states, as shown in Fig. 29 and Fig. 30, respectively.\nThe ˆSL gate implementation shown in Fig. 29 involves\ntwo logical CNOTs and two logical Hadamard opera-\n--- [Page 35] ---\n35\n〉 〉\nFIG. 29. Logic circuit that implements the ˆSL gate. The circuit uses the ancilla state |YL⟩ = (|gL⟩+i|eL⟩)/\n√\n2, on which\ntwo controlled logical CNOTs and two logical Hadamards are\nperformed, resulting in the input state |ψ L⟩ being transformed\nto ˆSL|ψ L⟩. Note that as ˆS†\nL = ˆZL ˆSL, the same circuit transforms |ψ L⟩ to ˆZL ˆS†\nL|ψ L⟩ where ˆZL is a byproduct operator.\ntions. An input state |ψL⟩ in one logical qubit is deterministically transformed into ˆSL|ψL⟩ by interacting\nwith the ancilla qubit in the |YL⟩ state."
