    "full": "⟩ of this circuit is\n|φL⟩ = ˆX pZ\nL ˆRZ ((−1)pZθ) |ψL⟩. (51)\nThe ﬁrst operator is a byproduct operator, whose power\npZ is equal to 0(1) if the ˆZL measurement MZ of the\nlogical qubit state is +1( −1). The second operator is a\nrotation by the angle θ,\nˆRZ(θ) =\n[ 1 0\n0 eiθ\n]\n. (52)\nFor the ˆTL gate, the rotation angle is θ = +π/4(−π/4)\ndepending on the sign +1( −1) of the ˆZL measurement.\nWe can test this circuit with the input state |ψ⟩ =\nα|g⟩ +β|e⟩ (dropping the L subscript) and the ancilla\nstate with θ = π/4 (this is the state |AL⟩). Hence the\ninitial state is\n(|g⟩ +eiπ/4|e⟩)|ψ⟩\n= α|gg⟩ +β|ge⟩ +eiπ/4α|eg⟩ +eiπ/4β|ee⟩.\n(53)\nThe CNOT transforms this to\nα|gg⟩ + β|ge⟩ +eiπ/4α|ee⟩ +eiπ/4β|eg⟩ =\n= ( α|g⟩ +eiπ/4β|e⟩)|g⟩ + (β|g⟩ +eiπ/4α|e⟩)|e⟩.\n(54)\nIf we measure the second qubit in |g⟩, i.e. we have the\noutcomeMZ = 1, the ﬁrst qubit state is α|g⟩+eiπ/4β|e⟩,\nwhich is precisely ˆTL|ψL⟩, so we have succeeded. If instead we measure the second qubit in |e⟩, i.e. the measurement outcome is MZ = −1, the ﬁrst qubit state is\nβ|g⟩ +eiπ/4α|e⟩ = ˆX\n(\neiπ/4α|g⟩ +β|e⟩\n)\n= eiπ/4 ˆX\n(\nα|g⟩ +βe−iπ/4|e⟩\n)\n,\n(55)\nwhich is ˆXL ˆT †\nL|ψL⟩ multiplied by an overall phase, which\ncan be neglected.\nHence approximately half of the times we run the circuit we will succeed in generating ˆTL|ψL⟩, signaled by\nthe measurement MZ = +1. However, the other times\nwe run the circuit the measurement MZ = −1 will signal\nthe output state\n|φL⟩ = ˆXL ˆRZ(−π/4)|ψL⟩ = ˆXL ˆT †\nL|ψL⟩."
