    "full": "in generating ˆTL|ψL⟩, signaled by\nthe measurement MZ = +1. However, the other times\nwe run the circuit the measurement MZ = −1 will signal\nthe output state\n|φL⟩ = ˆXL ˆRZ(−π/4)|ψL⟩ = ˆXL ˆT †\nL|ψL⟩. (56)\nIn this case, to achieve the desired result, we must ﬁx the\noutput using ˆSL ˆT †\nL = ˆTL. There is a slight complication\nif there are byproduct ˆXL or ˆZL operators, which we\ndiscuss in the next section; here we assume there are no\nbyproduct operators. The correction to the output is\nachieved by applying ˆSL to |φL⟩:\nˆSL|φL⟩ = ˆSL( ˆXL ˆT †\nL|ψL⟩)\n= ˆXL ˆS†\nL ˆT †\nL|ψL⟩\n= ˆXL( ˆZL ˆSL) ˆT †\nL|ψL⟩\n= ( ˆXL ˆZL) ˆTL|ψL⟩,\n(57)\nwhere we use the identity ˆSL ˆXL =i ˆXL ˆS†\nL and drop the\nunimportant phase factor of i. Hence passing the output state |φL⟩ through the ˆSL circuit gives the result\n( ˆXL ˆZL) ˆTL|ψL⟩, where ˆXL ˆZL are byproduct operators\nthat are handled by the control software.\nIf we need to perform ˆT †\nL, we use the circuit in Fig. 30,\nand about half the time we will get the measurement\noutcomeMZ = −1, which indicates the circuit produced\nˆXL ˆT †\nL, which is the desired output (with a byproduct\noperator ˆXL). The other half of the time we get the\nmeasurement outcome MZ = +1, and we can correct\n--- [Page 36] ---\n36\nAL SL TL\nIL\nXLZL\nFIG. 30. Logic circuit for the ˆTL gate. The circuit uses the\nancilla state |AL⟩ = ( |gL⟩ +eiπ/4|eL⟩)/\n√\n2, which is used to\ncontrol a CNOT on the target state |ψ L⟩, transforming the\nancilla to the output state |φ L⟩."
